PASS 1: the design's own list: eight domains, and the vault of record gives each one a case or a declared gap
PASS 2: contract: a vault is read only in its own shape
PASS 3: digest: independent of key order, changed by any pinned byte, case, gap or version
PASS 4: chain: versions are contiguous, each names the one before it, and a case leaves only by name
PASS 5: the vault of record: clean chain, pins equal the working tree and each script's whole grader closure
PASS 6: pins: one changed byte or a missing file is drift, and an invalid vault verifies nothing
PASS 7: gate: held only when every case is golden in the candidate tree
PASS 8: gate: one golden case red stops promotion, whatever else improved
PASS 9: gate: a baseline only says whose fault it is; it never rescues a red candidate
PASS 10: gate: what was not measured is never held
PASS 11: gate: a moved yardstick is not a comparison
PASS 12: path protection: the vault, what it pins, the eval yardstick and the owner constitution are never autonomous
